  "proposedChanges": [
    "Retain all 26 frozen components as exact current matches and add the current Chipotle Honey Chicken limited-time protein, producing a 27-product ingredient boundary.",
    "Treat High Protein Cups and curated High Protein meals as portion or composed presentations of already enumerated products, retaining presentation references without duplicating allergen-component identities.",
    "Preserve direct milk, soy, combined wheat/gluten, and vinegar-derived sulfite positives from the live official feed; products with empty API arrays remain unavailable instead of becoming supported negative claims.",
    "Add narrowly scoped may-contain gluten to Crispy Corn Tortilla, Roasted Chili-Corn Salsa, and Tortilla Chips from the restaurant's explicit corn co-mingling warning.",
    "Keep the general preparation-contact statement and the cannot-guarantee-absence language at restaurant level without converting them into universal item-level may-contain arrays.",
    "Keep Chipotle Honey Chicken allergen evidence unavailable because it is current but absent from the regular allergen feed and the official page warns that limited-time items may include allergens not listed there.",
    "Normalize Sofritas into the Proteins category and retain official API identifiers as presentation references rather than globally unique product identities."
